# Collaboration & Handoff

The goal: any contributor (human or AI) can pick up the project and get the same
behavior, because all context is versioned in the repo — not trapped in one
person's chat history.

## Everything shared lives in the repo

- Intent & knowledge: `.ai/**`
- Agent behavior: `.cursor/rules/**`, `AGENTS.md`
- Reusable workflows: `.cursor/commands/**`
- Quality gates: `.cursor/verify.json`, `.cursor/hooks/**`

Never rely on ephemeral chat memory or personal settings for anything a teammate
would need. If it matters, write it into one of the files above and commit it.

## Handing off work

- End every working session with `.ai/progress.md` updated: current state + the
  exact next step. A new agent should be able to run `/onboard` and continue.
- Record decisions as ADRs in `.ai/decisions/` so choices aren't re-litigated.
- Keep commits small and message the *why*.

## Consistency

- When behavior would contradict a recorded decision or convention, push back and
  cite the specific file instead of silently diverging.
